---
title: Local Conservation Nature Site
description: Market of Muir LCNS
headerImage: "/wcdt/wcdt-banner.avif"
headerAlt: "market of muir"
inContextNav: true
---

<!-- Clean, text-layered Hero Box -->
<section class="hero-header full-width">
  <div class="hero-bg-wrapper">
    <img src="/woodland/leaves.avif" alt="leaves bkg" width="1836" />
  </div>
  <!-- Wrap text in a layout alignment container -->
  <div class="hero-content">
    <p class="site-category">Local Conservation Nature Site</p>
    <h2>Biodiversity site: Market of Muir</h2>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Combined Layout Box for Description, Metrics, and Boundary Map -->
<div class="breakout grid-main-layout">
  <!-- Left Side Column: Text Narrative -->
  <section class="narrative">
    <h2>Site Description</h2>
    <p>
      Market of Muir is situated to the west of Westmuir and about 2km west of
      Kirriemuir in a predominantly agricultural area of lowland Angus.
      Extending to 31.6ha, the site is divided into three parts by two roads
      with the majority falling north of the A926 which is further divided by a
      minor road.
    </p>
    <p>
      The principal habitat is semi-natural broadleaved woodland which is
      considered <strong>locally rare</strong> and a
      <strong>UK Priority Habitat</strong>. Most of the site is dominated by
      birch woodland, some of which has been felled and replaced by Sitka
      spruce. Birch scrub separates the woodland from open areas containing
      remnants of wet and dry heath, and acid grassland communities.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the east of the site is an area of wet birch woodland and wet heath
      which is managed as <strong>Westmuir Community Woodland</strong>. This
      part of the site contains a formal path network.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Right Side Column: Boundary Data Card Stack & Map Display -->
  <div class="side-panel-stack">
    <section class="lncs-metrics">
      <h3>Site Boundary</h3>
      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <div class="metric-card">
          <span class="label">Grid Reference</span>
          <span class="value">NO362525</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card">
          <span class="label">Total Area</span>
          <span class="value">31.6 ha</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card">
          <span class="label">Elevation</span>
          <span class="value">100 - 160m</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="map-wrapper">
      <img
        src="/woodland/market-of-muir.avif"
        alt="market of muir boundary"
        width="1400"
      />
    </aside>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 3. ECOLOGY DATA: Standard content view, equal splitting -->
<section class="grid-2-col">
  <div class="data-block habitat-block">
    <h3>Habitats Present</h3>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Semi-natural broadleaved woodland</li>
      <li>Broadleaved & Coniferous plantation</li>
      <li>Continuous & Scattered scrub</li>
      <li>Marshy grassland & Acid grassland mosaic</li>
      <li>Dry & Wet dwarf shrub heath</li>
      <li>Open running water</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="data-block species-block">
    <h3>Species of Interest</h3>
    <p class="intro-text">
      A range of vascular plants, including locally rare varieties and Ancient
      Woodland Indicators:
    </p>
    <ul class="bullet-list special-species">
      <li>
        <strong>Lysimachia europaea</strong>
        <span class="common-name">(Chickweed wintergreen)</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pyrola minor</strong>
        <span class="common-name">(Common wintergreen)</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4. REGIONAL NETWORKS: Full width visual segment separating sections -->
<section class="full-width connectivity-banner">
  <div class="connectivity-content">
    <h2>Connectivity & Regional Networks</h2>
    <p>
      Market of Muir forms part of the Strathmore B-Lines network (Dunkeld –
      Montrose), offering high value as part of a habitat network connected in a
      wider context.
    </p>

    <div class="grid-4-col text-center">
      <div class="network-badge"><strong>Strathmore B-lines</strong> Link</div>
      <div class="network-badge">
        <strong>Egno Moss SSSI</strong> Contiguous
      </div>
      <div class="network-badge">
        <strong>Red Loch LNCS</strong> Connected via SSSI
      </div>
      <div class="network-badge">
        <strong>Loch of Kinnordy</strong> 0.83km away
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="full-width logo-container-wrapper">
  <div class="logo-grid">
    <div class="logo-item">
      <img
        eleventy:ignore
        src="/woodland/scottish-wildlife.svg"
        alt="Scottish Wildlife Trust"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="logo-item">
      <img
        src="/woodland/tayside-biodiversity.jpg"
        alt="Tayside Biodiversity"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="logo-item">
      <img eleventy:ignore src="/woodland/nature-scot.svg" alt="NatureScot" />
    </div>
    <div class="logo-item">
      <img
        eleventy:ignore
        src="/woodland/angus-council.svg"
        alt="Angus Council"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="logo-item">
      <img
        eleventy:ignore
        src="/woodland/bsbi-logo-rgb.svg"
        alt="Community Woodland"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Fixed Responsive Hero Configuration */
  .hero-header {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 14rem;
    max-height: 18rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: var(--primary, #1e3a2f);

    /* NEW: Force hero to inherit the main grid tracks */
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: inherit;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-bg-wrapper {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .hero-bg-wrapper img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: brightness(0.45);
  }

  /* 1. Set the mobile fallback layout track by default */
  .hero-header .hero-content {
    grid-column: content-start / content-end; /* Natively scales safely to 100% on phones */
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    color: white;
    padding-inline: var(
      --size-4,
      1rem
    ); /* Prevents the lettering from touching screen edges */
  }

  .hero-header .site-category {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin: 0;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .hero-header h2 {
    font-size: clamp(
      1.3rem,
      5vi,
      2.5rem
    ); /* Scaled down base slightly for thin phone frames */
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0 0;
    color: white;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  /* Layout Structure Containers */
  .grid-main-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--size-7, 40px);
    margin-block: var(--size-6);
  }

  .side-panel-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--size-5, 20px);
  }

  .lncs-metrics h3 {
    margin-block-end: var(--size-3);
  }

  .metrics-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--size-4, 16px);
    width: 100%;
  }

  /*
    OPUI THEMED METRIC CARD
    Flips background and dynamically swaps internal typography colors for perfect contrast
  */
  .metric-card {
    background: light-dark(var(--gray-3), var(--gray-11));
    color: light-dark(var(--gray-9), var(--gray-2));
    padding: var(--size-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-3, 8px);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--green-7, #2e5a44);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .metric-card .label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    color: light-dark(var(--gray-8), var(--gray-4));
  }

  .metric-card .value {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: light-dark(var(--green-8), var(--green-8));
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Map Container Layout Details */
  .map-wrapper {
    border-radius: var(--radius-3, 8px);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid light-dark(var(--gray-3), var(--gray-9));
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  }

  .map-wrapper img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Ecology Data and General Grid Components */
  .grid-2-col,
  .grid-4-col {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--size-5, 20px);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  /*
    OPUI THEMED DATA BLOCK
    Uses step surface shifts and matches border accents to the themes
  */
  .data-block {
    padding: var(--size-5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-3, 8px);
    background: light-dark(var(--gray-3), var(--gray-12));
    color: light-dark(var(--gray-9), var(--gray-2));
    box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid light-dark(var(--gray-2), var(--gray-11));
  }

  .habitat-block {
    border-top: 4px solid var(--green-6, #4a7c59);
  }
  .species-block {
    border-top: 4px solid var(--blue-6, #3d85c6);
  }

  .bullet-list {
    padding-left: var(--size-5);
  }
  .bullet-list li {
    margin-block-end: 0.5em;
  }
  .special-species li {
    list-style-type: "🌱 ";
  }

  .common-name {
    font-style: italic;
    color: light-dark(var(--gray-6), var(--gray-4));
  }

  /* Full-width Regional Connectivity Elements */
  .connectivity-banner {
    background-color: var(--green-11, #1e3a2f);
    color: white;
    padding-block: var(--size-7);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: inherit;
  }
  .connectivity-content {
    grid-column: content-start / content-end;
  }
  .connectivity-banner h2 {
    color: white;
  }

  .network-badge {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    color: white;
    padding: var(--size-3);
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* 2. Desktop Dynamic Scaling Viewport Promotes */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    /* Safe to expand typography to breakout width on wider viewports */
    .hero-header .hero-content {
      grid-column: breakout-start / breakout-end;
      padding-inline: 0; /* Remove internal padding once layout boundaries expand */
    }

    .grid-main-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 5fr 4fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .grid-2-col {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
    .grid-4-col {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .logo-container-wrapper {
    background-color: var(--gray-2);
    padding-block: 40px; /* Gives top and bottom breathing room before the next section */
    border-radius: 8px; /* Optional: Softens the edges of the gray block */
  }

  .logo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-items: center;

    /* Your exact sizing layout setup */
    inline-size: 80%;
    margin-inline: auto;

    /* Pro-tip addition: Prevents columns from getting too cramped on tiny phones */
    max-width: 1200px; /* Optional: Stops the logo bar from stretching infinitely on ultra-wide monitors */
  }

  /* For mobile devices, you can let it use more screen real estate if needed */
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .logo-grid {
      inline-size: 90%; /* Bumps it up slightly on tiny screens so logos stay legible */
    }
  }

  /* For tablets and larger screens (600px wide and up) */
  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .logo-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* For desktops (900px wide and up) -> Clean row of 5 columns */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .logo-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .logo-item img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 80px; /* Prevents taller logos from dominating the row */
    object-fit: contain; /* Keeps the logos from stretching out of shape */
  }
</style>
